# CAMEL OVERKILL: HUMP-P "POWER MANAGER". Four new batteries feed ONLY the engine and the two ballast pumps; the two
# vanilla batteries keep feeding the nav terminal, status monitor and gun capacitors (critical bus).
# ALL battery charging comes out of the reactor's surplus, so a battery suddenly charging can never brown out the main bus.
name camel_propulsion
box battery
note "HUMP-P POWER MANAGER: HOW IT WORKS" "Main bus demand = reactor load - battery charging, low-pass filtered (0.9 old + 0.1 new per tick; the two readings can arrive a tick apart). All charging flows through the CHARGE TAP relay, whose load_value_out is exactly what the batteries draw.\nWanted charge: propulsion = its bus load + (80 - charge %) x 40 kW (0..2000), so it hovers at 80 %; critical = (100 - charge %) x 40 kW (0..1000), kept full.\nReactor setpoint (out2 -> HUMP-1) = main demand + both wants + 1000 kW while the governor is about to switch the oxygen generator on (7212).\nSurplus = reactor output - main demand. Critical bank takes min(surplus, its want), propulsion takes the rest. HUMP-R (second box) turns the two shares into battery rates. So when the reactor lags behind a step the charging gives way instead of the voltage, and a sudden drop in load is soaked up.\nPropulsion below 25 % -> 1 on 7209 (alert YELLOW). Telemetry: 7202 propulsion charge %, 7211 propulsion kW."
note "WIRING" "in1 charge_%, in2 load_value_out from ONE propulsion battery\nin4 <- CHARGE TAP relay load_value_out\nin5 charge_% from ONE critical (vanilla) battery\nin3 reactor load_value_out, in6 reactor power_value_out\nout1 -> HUMP-R in1 (critical share kW), out5 -> HUMP-R in2 (propulsion share kW)\nout3 -> disable_output of every propulsion battery (held 0)\nout2 -> HUMP-1 in8 (setpoint kW)"
c txc wifi Channel=7202
c txl wifi Channel=7211
c txw wifi Channel=7209
c k25 mem Value=25
c low greater
w k25.out low.1
w low.out txw.in
# --- main bus demand = reactor load - battery charging (measured by the CHARGE TAP relay that feeds both banks)
c base00 sub
w in3 base00.1
w in4 base00.2
# the oxygen generator (1000 kW) switches in one tick: take it out of the filter and add it back from the relay
# command itself (7213), so a switch-off is soaked up by the batteries at once instead of 0.3 s later
c rxg wifi Channel=7213
c k1000 mem Value=1000
c gkw mul
w rxg.out gkw.1
w k1000.out gkw.2
c base0 sub
w base00.out base0.1
w gkw.out base0.2
# low-pass for the reactor setpoint (x 0.9 old + 0.1 new per tick): the two loads can arrive a tick apart
c base mem Value=0
c f9 mem Value=0.9
c f1 mem Value=0.1
c bo mul
c bn mul
c bs add
w base.out bo.1
w f9.out bo.2
w base0.out bn.1
w f1.out bn.2
w bo.out bs.1
w bn.out bs.2
w bs.out base.in
c basef add
w base.out basef.1
w gkw.out basef.2
# --- wants
c k80 mem Value=80
c k100 mem Value=100
c kg mem Value=40
c errp sub
c biasp mul
c wantp add ClampMin=0 ClampMax=2000
w k80.out errp.1
w in1 errp.2 low.2 txc.in
w errp.out biasp.1
w kg.out biasp.2
w in2 wantp.1 txl.in
w biasp.out wantp.2
c errc sub
c biasc mul ClampMin=0 ClampMax=1000
w k100.out errc.1
w in5 errc.2
w errc.out biasc.1
w kg.out biasc.2
# --- setpoint
c rxo wifi Channel=7212
c pre mul
w rxo.out pre.1
w k1000.out pre.2
c sp1 add
c sp2 add
c sp3 add
w basef.out sp1.1
w wantp.out sp1.2
w sp1.out sp2.1
w biasc.out sp2.2
w sp2.out sp3.1
w pre.out sp3.2
w sp3.out out2
# --- share the surplus: critical first (min(surplus, want)), propulsion gets the rest
c sur sub
w in6 sur.1
w basef.out sur.2
c md sub
c ma abs
c ms add
c mm sub
c k2 mem Value=2
c cmin div ClampMin=0
w sur.out md.1 ms.1
w biasc.out md.2 ms.2
w md.out ma.in
w ms.out mm.1
w ma.out mm.2
w mm.out cmin.1
w k2.out cmin.2
c zero mem Value=0
c rest sub
w sur.out rest.1
w cmin.out rest.2
c restc add ClampMin=0 ClampMax=2000
w rest.out restc.1
w zero.out restc.2
w cmin.out out1          # critical bank's share (kW) -> HUMP-R in1
w restc.out out5         # propulsion bank's share (kW) -> HUMP-R in2
